{title: 581 - When the Church of Jesus}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #581 • KING'S WESTON • 11.11.12.11}
{lyricist: Fred Pratt Green}
{composer: Ralph Vaughan Williams}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 581}
{meta: tune KING'S WESTON}
{meta: meter 11.11.12.11}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]When the church [C]of [Dm]Jesus shuts its [C7]outer [Dm]door,
[F/A]Lest the roar of [Am/C]traffic [Dm]drown the voice [Gm/Bb]of [F/A]prayer:
[C]May our [Gm/Bb]prayers, [C]Lord [Am]make up [Dm]ten [C/E]times [F]more [Gm]aware
[Dm/F]That the [C/E]world we banish [Am/C]is [F]our Christian [C]care.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]If our hearts [C]are [Dm]lifted where devotion soars
[F/A]High above this [Am/C]hungry [Dm]suffering [Gm/Bb]world [F/A]of [Gm]ours:
[C]Lest our [Gm/Bb]hymns [C]should [Am]drug us [Dm]to [C/E]forget [F]its [Gm]needs,
[Dm/F]Forge our [C/E]Christian worship [Am/C]into [F]Christian [C]deeds.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]Lest the gifts [C]we [Dm]offer, money, [C7]talents, [Dm]time,
[F/A]Serve to salve our [Am/C]conscience [Dm]to our secret [F/A]shame:
[C]Lord, reprove, inspire [Am/C]us [Dm]by [C/E]the way [F]you [Gm]give;
[Dm/F]Teach us, [C/E]dying Savior, [Am/C]how [F]true Christians [C]live.
{end_of_verse}
